Time complexity(efficiency) - example - google search engine (PageRank algorithm)
 Order of growth = Orders of Growth ka matlab hota hai ki jab input size bahut bada ho jaye, tab program ka runtime kitni speed se grow karega. Ye mainly Big-O notation me express kiya jata hai.

Goals / Main Points:
Jab input bahut bada ho, tab program kitna efficient hai ye check karna.
Program ka runtime input size ke saath kaise increase hota hai, usko represent karna.
Runtime growth ka ek upper bound nikalna (maximum possible growth).
Hume exact time nahi chahiye, sirf “order of growth” chahiye.
Example: exact 102 ms nahi, bas ye ki runtime O(n) hai ya O(n²).
Hum program ke largest factor ko dekhte hain:
Kaunsa part sabse zyada time lega?
Isliye generally hum:
Worst case me tight upper bound find karte hain as function of input size.
 
 Simple Example
1. Linear Growth
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)

Yaha loop n times chalega.

Time Complexity:

O(n)

f(n)=n

2. Quadratic Growth
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
   for(int j=0; j<n; j++)

Nested loops hain, total operations:

n×n=n
2

Time Complexity:

O(n2)

f(n)=n
2

Common Orders of Growth
Complexity	Meaning
O(1)	Constant time
O(log n)	Logarithmic
O(n)	Linear
O(n log n)	Efficient sorting
O(n²)	Nested loops
O(2^n)	Exponential 

recursion :- Recursion ek programming technique hai jisme ek function khud ko hi baar-baar call karta hai kisi problem ko chhote parts me solve karne ke liye. Ye process tab tak chalta hai jab tak base case (stop condition) meet na ho jaye.

list - ordered mutable collection of item.

slicing :- Slicing Python ki ek technique hai jisse hum string, list ya tuple ka koi specific part (portion) nikal sakte hain.

iterate :- "Kisi list, string, tuple ya kisi collection ke har element ko ek-ek karke access karne ki process ko Iteration (Iterate) kehte hain."

enumerate :- "enumerate() ek function hai jo iterable (list, tuple, string, etc.) ke har element ke saath uska index bhi return karta hai."

comprehension :- Comprehension Python ki ek short aur efficient technique hai jisse ek hi line me nayi list, set ya dictionary create ki ja sakti hai, bina normal for loop ko alag se likhe.

 nested list comprehension :- Nested Loop Comprehension ka matlab hai ek hi comprehension ke andar ek se zyada for loops ka use karna, jisse multiple loops ka kaam ek hi line me ho jata hai.

set(mutable) :- "Set ek collection hai jo sirf unique elements ko store karta hai aur duplicate values ko automatically remove kar deta hai."

subset method :- Agar Set A ke har element, Set B me bhi ho, to A ko B ka subset kehte hain.

shallow copy :- Shallow Copy ek aisi copy hoti hai jisme outer object ka naya copy banta hai, lekin andar ke nested (inner) objects original object ke saath hi shared rehte hain.

 Itrating over dictionaries :- "Kisi collection ke elements ko one by one access ya process karne ki process ko Iterating kehte hain."
# you can use loops to iterative over dictonatries, keys , values or items

Dictionary comprehension :- Comprehension Python ki ek shortcut technique hai jisse ek hi line me for loop aur optional if condition ka use karke naya collection (List, Set, ya Dictionary) banaya jata hai.

lambda function : Lambda functions are small anonymous functions defined using a Lambda keyword. They can have any number of arguments but only one expression. They are commonly used for short operations or as arguments to higher order function .

Map() function :- The map() function applies a given function to all the items in an input list (or any other iterable) and returns a map object (an iterator). This is particularly useful for transforming data in a list comprehensively.

filter() funtion : filter() Python ka built-in function hai jo kisi iterable (list, tuple, etc.) se sirf un elements ko return karta hai jo di gayi condition ko satisfy karte hain.

Pseudocode 
1. A pseudocode simple way of describing an algorithm in plain language or a mix of code like and natural language instructions.
2. It doesn't follow any specific  programming language syntax making it easier to understanding even for those without programming language.
3. pseudocode is often  used as a step before writing  actual code.

Process to solve a problem
1. Analyze your problem      --    input, output, constraint 
2. Breakdown problem into smaller subports.
3. Remember/ enlist the concept.
4. Tore 2-3 examples.        --    Clear out confusion / gap 
Write a paeudocode on the paper.

Array : -> An array is a collection of elements stored in  categous memory location.
-> all elements of are the same data type (integer float etc.)
-> array  allow for efficient access and manipulation of data.

1. Linear Search

Linear Search is a searching algorithm that checks each element one by one until the target element is found or the list ends.

Hinglish: List ke har element ko ek-ek karke check karta hai.

2. Binary Search

Binary Search is a searching algorithm that searches a sorted list by repeatedly dividing it into two halves.

Hinglish: Sorted list ko baar-baar do hisson me baant kar element dhoondta hai.

3. Bubble Sort

Bubble Sort is a sorting algorithm that repeatedly compares adjacent elements and swaps them if they are in the wrong order.

Hinglish: Paas-paas ke elements compare karta hai aur galat order me hone par swap karta hai.

4. Selection Sort

Selection Sort is a sorting algorithm that repeatedly selects the smallest element from the unsorted part and places it at the correct position.

Hinglish: Unsorted list me se sabse chhota element select karke uski sahi position par rakhta hai.

5. Insertion Sort

Insertion Sort is a sorting algorithm that builds the sorted list by inserting one element at a time into its correct position.

Hinglish: Ek-ek element ko uski sahi jagah insert karke sorted list banata hai.

6. Merge Sort

Merge Sort is a divide-and-conquer sorting algorithm that divides the list into halves, sorts them, and merges them back.

Hinglish: List ko chhote parts me divide karke sort karta hai aur phir merge karta hai.

7. Quick Sort

Quick Sort is a divide-and-conquer sorting algorithm that selects a pivot element and partitions the list around it.

Hinglish: Pivot choose karke uske according list ko partition karta hai aur recursively sort karta hai.

8. Heap Sort

Heap Sort is a sorting algorithm that uses a heap data structure to repeatedly remove the largest (or smallest) element.

Hinglish: Heap data structure ka use karke elements ko sort karta hai.

9. Counting Sort

Counting Sort is a non-comparison sorting algorithm that sorts elements by counting the occurrences of each value.

Hinglish: Har value kitni baar aayi hai usko count karke sorting karta hai.

10. Radix Sort

Radix Sort is a non-comparison sorting algorithm that sorts numbers digit by digit from least significant to most significant digit.

Hinglish: Numbers ko digit-by-digit sort karta hai.

11. Searching

Searching is the process of finding a specific element in a collection of data.

Hinglish: Data me kisi specific element ko dhoondhne ki process.

12. Sorting

Sorting is the process of arranging data in ascending or descending order.

Hinglish: Data ko ascending ya descending order me arrange karna.

